AIM: Develop programs for numeric analysis using numpy. 
1) NumPy program to test whether none of the elements of a given array is zero. 
SOURCE CODE: 
import numpy as np 
x = np.array([1,2,3,4]) 
print("Original Array:") 
print(x) 
print("Test if none of the elements of the said array is zero:") 
print(np.all(x)) 
x = np.array([0,1,2,3]) 
print("Original Array:") 
print(x) 
print("Test if none of the elements of the said array is zero:") 
print(np.all(x)) 
 
 
 
2) NumPy program to test whether any of the elements of a given array is non-zero. 
SOURCE CODE: 
import numpy as np 
x = np.array([1,0,0,0]) 
print("Original Array:") 
print(x) 
print("Test whether any of the elements of a given array is non zero:") 
print(np.any(x)) 
x = np.array([0,0,0,0]) 
print("Original Array:") 
print(x) 
print("Test any of the elements of a given array is non zero:") 
